WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.640
The SCP Foundation’s most famous anomalies
are legendary.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:11.060
From the notorious 682 in its acid bath to
Pesterbot, some SCPs are instantly recognizable

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:14.730
from only an image or a few sentences of information.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:20.480
But the SCP Foundation also encompasses endless
universes and possibilities, and that means

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.829
endless variations on these iconic anomalies.

00:00:24.829 --> 00:00:31.300
Maybe in one reality 173 is simply one of
many terrifying statutes, or perhaps 682 is

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.440
a heir to the infamous infernal Scarlet King.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.400
And of course, there are other versions of
the Foundation itself too!

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:43.000
From worlds where they are known as the Foundation
Incorporated, and seek only to line their

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:48.120
own pockets, to realities where the Foundation
is a theocratic organization holding the line

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.850
after the apocalypse.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:54.470
What follows is a peek into one such alternate
universe, and their version of one of the

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:58.680
Foundation’s most mysterious and enigmatic
anomalies.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.690
Can you guess what it is?

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:05.390
Some people think the Foundation’s operations
are limited to the land, air, and sea.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:09.960
To some extent, they’re right - while the
vast majority of anomalies exist on Earth,

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:15.690
the O5 Council knows that space is infinite
and that means infinite possibilities for

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:16.690
anomalies.

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:22.700
That’s why the Foundation has sites on the
Moon, on space stations orbiting Earth, even

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:25.710
installations on Venus and Mars.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:30.000
There are even rumors that the Foundation
retains their very own small fleet of space

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.920
shuttles to move some of the particularly
dangerous anomalies off-planet where they

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.600
pose no risk to society.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:41.190
But space goes well beyond just our neighboring
planets.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:46.310
The Foundation also invests heavily into exploring
deep space, so that they might find anomalies

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:49.760
like the Hateful Star before they pose a danger
rather than after.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:54.940
To this end, they’ve sent a small army of
space probes, equipped with advanced sensors

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:59.979
and rudimentary artificial intelligence, in
every direction away from our planet to scout

00:01:59.979 --> 00:02:02.020
for potential anomalies.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:07.850
But the issue is that sometimes the probes
actually end up encountering anomalies.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:13.670
Such is the curious case of Probe H9, which
disappeared under mysterious circumstances

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:19.190
while scouting a potential anomaly in a completely
empty, barren region of deep space.

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:24.950
The Foundation assigns an internal investigator
to the case - one Geoffrey Davies, who schedules

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:29.980
a sit-down with Isaac Miles, the chief technician
in charge of the probe and many others under

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:31.760
Foundation command.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:37.080
Probe H9’s AI system, known as PH9, was
in communication with Miles throughout its

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.790
strange journey, right up until the end.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:42.260
The logs, requested by Davies, are read out.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.180
At first, it seems like a routine signal.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:50.590
PH9 calls in to base to inform them it has
detected a signal - but not just any signal,

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:56.680
an emergency SOS signal coming from deep in
an otherwise-empty quadrant of space.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:02.300
Despite having two sensors, the probe is unable
to find anything in that area with its telescope.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:06.349
Miles authorizes the probe to change its route
to pass through where the signal is coming

00:03:06.349 --> 00:03:14.370
from, and PH9 confirms that it will arrive
at the source of the SOS in 399 hours, or

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.370
17 days.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:17.350
The two men exchange some words.

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:23.040
Miles explains he did not contact his superiors
because protocol means they need visual confirmation

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:28.630
before sending a space shuttle in – and
PH9’s telescope couldn’t find anything.

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:33.069
Even though the signal was confirmed to be
human, Miles didn’t want to break protocol,

00:03:33.069 --> 00:03:35.940
and let the probe go in alone.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:40.360
Investigator Davies begrudgingly agrees that
it was a smart decision, and they move on.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:44.990
An hour after PH9 entered the quadrant of
space where the signal was coming from, Miles

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:47.401
is still waiting for a report.

00:03:47.401 --> 00:03:51.780
Finally, he contacts PH9, which informs him
that it is still unable to get a look at where

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:57.580
the signal is coming from, even though it
is so close it will arrive in 4 hours.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:03.349
Miles, confused by how this is possible, asks
it for readings on its weight and gravity.

00:04:03.349 --> 00:04:08.470
The Investigator asks him why he wanted this
information and Miles explains that the probe

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:10.990
‘passed through some kind of event horizon’.

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:15.209
The probe was continuing to move into the
quadrant, but for some reason looked like

00:04:15.209 --> 00:04:16.329
it wasn’t.

00:04:16.329 --> 00:04:21.620
This happens when something enters a black
hole, but if it was a black hole PH9 would’ve

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:25.190
been unable to transmit and completely destroyed.

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:30.650
Some kind of anomaly had trapped PH9 inside
its massive well of gravity.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:36.050
When Miles again radioed into PH9, the probe
had a strange response: that it would pass

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:41.340
by the signal source in 4 hours, the exact
same as last time.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:46.870
Something was obviously wrong with the probe,
as well over 4 hours had passed and the probe’s

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:49.770
signal meant it should be right next to the
source.

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:56.000
Miles decides the probe is faulty, and assigns
Probe J4 to meet it and take it to a repair

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.000
facility.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.970
But when Probe J4 arrives, PH9 can’t see
it.

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:04.900
PH9 can’t even detect it using any other
kind of sensor.

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:11.669
But it does detect the same SOS signal, and
against all logic, it’s still 4 hours away.

00:05:11.669 --> 00:05:16.880
PH9 tries to offer its coordinates, but it
can’t - in fact, it says that its current

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:22.750
coordinates are ‘outside of Euclidean space’,
like so many non-Euclidean anomalies the Foundation

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:23.750
deals with.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:28.540
Miles can’t decide whether PH9 has fallen
into a gravity well or something much, much

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:32.510
worse has happened, and PH9 holds position.

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:37.210
Miles explains that then, he called his superiors
to let them know the deeply strange events

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:41.900
occurring in relation to their probes, but
the closest team was a week away - by the

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:45.210
time they arrived on scene to investigate,
it was all over.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:49.620
They couldn’t advise on what to do about
the probe - there were far too many unknowns

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.870
in relation to space anomalies.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:57.539
And so Miles simply told PH9 to continue on
its course and report back every hour, because

00:05:57.539 --> 00:06:00.820
there was nothing else to do and nothing to
lose.

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:04.880
The last hour of reports are where things
suddenly take a sharp turn.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:09.509
PH9 calls in to command, saying that it is
suddenly detecting a massive object almost

00:06:09.509 --> 00:06:11.600
a million kilometres away from it.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:16.830
The signal source is still 4 hours away, but
this new object is some sort of planetoid,

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:21.430
1400 kilometres across and incredibly light
for its size.

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:25.610
For comparison, the asteroid that killed the
dinosaurs was 10 kilometers across.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:31.889
PH9 moves to get a better look, but its analysis
keeps failing - because it’s getting closer.

00:06:31.889 --> 00:06:34.520
Not just that, but getting closer impossibly
quickly.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:38.169
In a minute, it’s suddenly 400,000 kilometres
away.

00:06:38.169 --> 00:06:44.090
Thirty seconds later and it’s 250,000km
and showing no signs of slowing down.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:48.960
Before Miles can explain why this is impossible,
the probe reports it is about to collide with

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:50.070
the planetoid.

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:55.350
The last message it transmits before all communications
cease is a single image from its telescope,

00:06:55.350 --> 00:07:01.009
showing whatever was about to crash into the
probe: a massive, blurry white sphere, completely

00:07:01.009 --> 00:07:03.479
featureless against the starless backdrop.

00:07:03.479 --> 00:07:05.790
The men are confused.

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:09.789
Neither of them know what this image means
- by all evidence, the probe was rocketing

00:07:09.789 --> 00:07:13.490
through empty space way too fast for anything
to catch up to it.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:18.759
And yet, something obviously did - something
was chasing the probe.

00:07:18.759 --> 00:07:23.330
They agree it wasn’t a rogue planet, and
Davies dismisses Miles with some words of

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:28.889
advice: to start taking his vacation time
and head on home after a final debriefing.

00:07:28.889 --> 00:07:33.050
Turning to his aide, he instructs the agent
to file the interview and completely quarantine

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:37.970
that quadrant of space, making sure nothing
enters or exits.

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:41.789
And, ominously, to ensure that Miles gets
‘processed’.

00:07:41.789 --> 00:07:45.479
The Foundation does not leave loose ends untied
after all.

00:07:45.479 --> 00:07:49.630
Have you managed to figure out what anomaly
this is a parallel version of?

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:54.270
Something going into a contained endless space,
towards a human signal at the bottom that

00:07:54.270 --> 00:08:00.120
seems to never be getting closer, before suddenly
being consumed by a blurry white thing?

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:07.800
That’s right, it’s the infamous and notorious
SCP-087, the Endless Staircase.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:12.289
Many of us are familiar with this anomaly
- we should be, considering how dangerous

00:08:12.289 --> 00:08:16.190
and ominous it is to even seasoned Foundation
veterans.

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:23.039
A metal door in the back of a high school
campus, leading down… and down… and down,

00:08:23.039 --> 00:08:28.449
endlessly into an inky black void with a bone
chilling weeping and crying of a baby coming

00:08:28.449 --> 00:08:32.610
from the bottom, teasing people to try and
find the source.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:36.699
At first the Foundation were only interested
in finding out where exactly this crying was

00:08:36.699 --> 00:08:42.649
coming from - but soon, they realized, just
like Miles, that something was very, very

00:08:42.649 --> 00:08:43.649
wrong.

00:08:43.649 --> 00:08:48.569
The first explorer they sent in, an older
man, had gone down only a few flights when

00:08:48.569 --> 00:08:51.959
he heard the crying and sobbing of a baby
200m away.

00:08:51.959 --> 00:08:58.360
Spooked, he was instructed against his protests
to continue descending the dark, damp staircase.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:03.670
Almost 30 flights down, he suddenly realized
the next landing wasn’t empty like the others

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:09.410
In front of him was a grotesque parody of
a head - an alabaster white face with no mouth

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:13.769
or nostrils and blank, empty white eyes.

00:09:13.769 --> 00:09:17.619
Just floating feet above the ground, staring
at that thing.

00:09:17.619 --> 00:09:23.160
Despite his terror, the subject began to approach
- just before it suddenly shot up the stairs,

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:24.970
going right for his face.

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:28.999
By the time he reached the top of the stairs
after a panicked, hysterical run, he collapsed

00:09:28.999 --> 00:09:31.129
face down on the concrete.

00:09:31.129 --> 00:09:33.499
The Foundation’s following attempts fared
little better.

00:09:33.499 --> 00:09:37.910
In one, the D-class had descended almost 100
flights of stairs when he encountered the

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:38.910
face.

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:43.129
Doing nothing, they simply stared at each
other - right up until the face again shot

00:09:43.129 --> 00:09:44.259
up toward him.

00:09:44.259 --> 00:09:47.959
He turned and ran, screaming all the way up
the stairs.

00:09:47.959 --> 00:09:53.629
Unlike the first subject, he didn’t manage
to make it out of SCP-087 before he collapsed.

00:09:53.629 --> 00:09:58.350
His heart stopped and the Foundation prepared
to send in a recovery mission - until, suddenly,

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:03.899
his heart restarted, but with an abnormal,
unnatural heartbeat.

00:10:03.899 --> 00:10:08.889
The subject’s limp form then calmly walked
up the stairs to the exit, closed the door,

00:10:08.889 --> 00:10:14.230
sat down, and fell into a vegetative state,
slipping into a permanent coma.

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:18.449
In the next, everything seemed to be going
well, until the subject encountered a strange

00:10:18.449 --> 00:10:21.309
hole in the landing with a light at the bottom.

00:10:21.309 --> 00:10:26.660
Shrugging, she continues, all the way to the
500th landing, almost two kilometers below

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:30.019
ground, when she decides to go back up against
orders.

00:10:30.019 --> 00:10:35.100
Turning around, she is shocked by the presence
of the face only a few inches behind her head.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:39.149
It had been following her down those stairs
for who-knows-how-long.

00:10:39.149 --> 00:10:44.639
And this time, it’s not staring at her - it’s
staring at the researchers behind the screens

00:10:44.639 --> 00:10:45.639
of her camera.

00:10:45.639 --> 00:10:50.970
In terror, she runs down the stairs, looking
behind her after several hundred feet - only

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:56.170
to see the face still barely a foot behind
her, staring into the camera with a dead-eyed

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:57.170
glare.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:11:01.170
By the time she realizes that the sound of
the crying is getting closer, she has already

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:06.329
stumbled and fallen down into the hard concrete,
knocking herself unconscious.

00:11:06.329 --> 00:11:11.049
The last thing the researchers see before
the camera cuts out is the face making piercing

00:11:11.049 --> 00:11:13.160
eye contact with them.

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:17.889
And of course, the infamous fourth exploration.

00:11:17.889 --> 00:11:23.610
Whatever occurred in this final descent into
SCP-087 was so concerning to the Foundation

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:27.829
that they opted to seal all logs of it and
expunge all the data.

00:11:27.829 --> 00:11:32.569
We may never truly know what lies at the bottom
of the staircase or what the face wants from

00:11:32.569 --> 00:11:38.050
people who enter its territory, just like
how we may never know what exactly Probe H9

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:42.970
was being signalled by, or what the massive
object moving at the speed of light directly

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.980
into the probe was.

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:49.899
And just like how the Foundation cleaned up
all the remains of Exploration IV, the Foundation

00:11:49.899 --> 00:11:56.190
also plans to make sure Miles cannot tell
anyone about this strange deep-space anomaly.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:12:01.720
Now check out “SCP-1548 - The Star, the
Hateful” for another space based anomaly,

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:08.459
or for more from the depths of SCP-087 watch
“The Secret at the Bottom of SCP-087 - EXPLAINED”

